-- Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood - its bestiary and its notable NPCs.
-- 2 creatures (migration 074) and 0 notable NPCs (migration 072),
-- with their attacks in stat_attacks (migration 073).
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/~082-wormwood-host-and-dark-priest.sql
--
-- Written by scripts/bestiary-sql.mjs from 1 worker file(s). Every
-- creature row passes creatureFormulaGaps, every value is printable ASCII,
-- and an 8-word shingle check of the prose fields against the book's cached text finds no copied run.

INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES
('dark-priest', 'Dark Priest', 'humanoid', 'rifts', 0, 'Must be anarchist or evil: approximately 15% anarchist, 35% miscreant, 35% diabolic and 15% aberrant', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '1D4x10+40', NULL, 'No attribute dice are printed: ''typical attributes'' are average to high I.Q., M.A. and/or M.E., and 60% of dark priests have average to low P.S., P.P., P.E. and Spd; P.B. ranges from 3 to 30. P.P.E. is a permanent base of 1D4x10+40 plus 2D6 per level; it recovers 4 points per hour of rest or 10 per hour of meditation. M.D.C.: the O.C.C. adds +30 M.D.C. (S.D.C. in non-magic-rich environments) plus 1D6 per level of experience on top of the character''s own base, which this entry does not print, so no M.D.C. formula is stored. When possessed by the Unholy or one of the Host: +300 M.D.C./hit points, P.S. raised to 40, +1 on all saving throws, sees the invisible, and has every communion with Wormwood spell the Host knows.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'O.C.C. bonuses: +4 save vs horror factor, +4 save vs supernatural and psionic possession. Hand to Hand: Basic (expert for one ''other'' skill; assassin or martial arts for two). Skill bonuses are halved if I.Q. is six or less. Resin chain mail or light armor gives 40 M.D.C. with no prowl penalty.', 'O.C.C. Skills: Lore: Monsters & Demons (+20%), Lore: Wormwood (25% + 5% per level), Language: American (+30%), Language: Demongogian (98%), Language: Gobblely (90%), Literacy: American (+20%), Math: Basic (+20%), Biology (+10%), Prowl (+5%), W.P. Knife, W.P. two of choice, Hand to Hand: Basic. Six ''other'' skills plus one more at levels three, six, nine and twelve; four secondary skills. Levels: the average dark priest is third to fifth; medium sixth to ninth; high priests tenth or higher; young priests first and second.', 'A mortal villain rather than a monster: its strength is prayer-fueled communion magic, healing from injury twice as fast as ordinary folk through meditation, and the option of letting the Unholy or a Host ride its body as a supernaturally strong warlord while the possessor''s own body lies comatose under guard. From third level it is given a small retinue of beast guards, air fish or demon goblins, plus two tick parasites to guard its home.', 'Communion with Wormwood, starting powers: Close an Opening, Create a Burial Place, Create a Fountain of Water, Create Life Force Cauldron, Create Magic Slime, Create an Opening, Create Worm Zombies, Mold Structures, Ride Giant Parasites, Summon and Command Parasites, Summon Flies. One additional ability at levels one, two, four and six; two additional at levels three, five and seven; one at each level after. Cannot draw P.P.E. from other beings except by blood sacrifice or when another priest offers it. Carries four different magic slime potions, 1D4+1 magic slime ointments and one lesser blood stone.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Wormwood, in the cities and armies of the Forces of Darkness', 'The Unholy; Forces of Darkness', 'Priests of light, the Cathedral, the knights of the Temple and the Champions of Light', NULL, 'A human or D-bee who has sold out to the Host for power, wealth or the pleasure of cruelty, and who ranks just under the Host and the demon lords in running Wormwood. The dark mirror of the priests of light, it corrupts, slanders and assassinates the planet''s champions while commanding men, parasites and demons. It dresses in a red robe edged with black and gold and a spiked red hood. A non-player villain O.C.C.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.117-119'),
('host', 'The Host', 'demon', 'rifts', 0, 'Diabolic or miscreant only', '{"IQ":"2D6+13","ME":"2D6+13","MA":"2D6+13","PS":"4D6+20","PP":"2D6+13","PE":"2D6+13","PB":"2D4","Spd":"6D6"}', NULL, NULL, '1D4x1000+2D4x100', '2D4x100', '2D4x100', 'Spd 6D6 is running; flying speed is 1D4x10+50. P.S. is supernatural. M.D.C./Hit Points is printed as 1D4x1000, with 2D4x100 added for the average Host whenever three or more Host are in the same world; Wormwood has 19, so the stored formula includes that addition. The one leader (the Unholy) gets a further 4D6x100 M.D.C., +10 P.S., +300 P.P.E., +200 I.S.P., Horror Factor 19, two more attacks per melee (7 total), +1 save vs psionic attacks and all magic, and is 20% larger. Bio-regenerates 1D6x100 M.D.C. once every five minutes.', NULL, 17, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":1,"strike":6,"parry":5,"dodge":5,"roll":4,"pull":4}', 'Five attacks per melee by hand to hand or psionics, or two by magic; combat equal to hand to hand: expert. Critical strike on unmodified 18-20; the finger claws count as paired weapons. +1 save vs psionics, +3 save vs spell and illusionary magic, +2 save vs circle magic, +10 save vs horror factor. Limitations: cannot swim (sinks and drowns), and holy water burns it as it does a vampire. The four eyes cannot be regenerated: a called shot at -4 hits a large eye, -6 a tiny one.', 'Minimal: can learn to read and write up to four languages and 1D4 other technical skills, and knows at 85% basic math, literacy in American, land navigation, streetwise, cryptography, forgery, palming, concealment, prowl, dance and horsemanship: monsters. Level of experience 6th to 9th (1D4+5); the leader is 10th to 13th (1D4+9). Spell, communion and psionic strength equal that level.', 'Shrugs off poisons, toxins, drugs and gases and ordinary fire (magic fire and plasma do half); nightvision 1000 ft (305 m), sees the invisible and into the ultraviolet; tracks by smell 60% and by blood scent 80%; flies on bat wings; the torso is plated in heavy natural armor; regrows lost limbs within 72 hours, though never an eye. Where three or more Host hold sway the land itself turns twisted and diseased. Can only enter a world by permanently taking over a willing mortal''s body, and dies at once if it ever leaves that world.', 'Communion with Wormwood: Close an Opening, Create Life Force Cauldron, Create Magic Slime, Create an Opening, Create a Pillar, Create Stairs, Create Tunnel, Create Wall, Create Worm Zombies, Destroy Life Force Cauldron, Impervious to Symbiotes, Mold Structures, Open & Close Dimensional Rifts, Remove Symbiotes, Repel Symbiotes, Ride Giant Parasites, Summon Entities, Summon and Command Parasites, Summon & Use Symbiotes. Off Wormwood the same power instead grants: globe of daylight, chameleon, fear, breathe without air, fingers of wind, wind rush, fool''s gold, repel animals, animate and control dead, life drain, eyes of the wolf, summon and control canines, summon and control rodents, summon and control insects, summon fog. Likely to own 1D6 magic weapons; never uses symbiotes.', 'Master psionic: astral projection, clairvoyance, empathy, telepathy, see aura, total recall, detect psionics, psychic diagnosis, psychic surgery, healing touch, deaden pain, sleep, mind block auto-defense, group mind block, bio-manipulation, empathic transmission, hypnotic suggestion, mentally possess others, psi-sword and one super psionic power of choice.', '10 to 13 feet tall (3 to 3.96 m); the leader is 20% larger, roughly 15 feet (4.6 m)', '1200 pounds (540 kg)', '2D4x1000 years or until slain', 'Wormwood, where 19 of them rule as generals, governors and kings; about 10,000 more remain trapped in their prison dimension', 'The Unholy; Forces of Darkness', NULL, NULL, 'The lesser kin of the Unholy: wolf-headed, bull-horned and bull-legged, bat-winged giants with gaunt, bony arms and grey-pink skin, who serve as the ruling elite of Wormwood''s dark empire. These are the figures for an average Host; the Unholy, High Lord Lesion and Lord Krikton have their own entries.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.138-141');

